    <item>
      <title>Nutch 1.20 Release</title>
      <link>/news/nutch-1.20-release/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 25 Apr 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>/news/nutch-1.20-release/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href=&#34;https://projects.apache.org/committee.html?nutch&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34;&gt;Apache Nutch PMC&lt;/a&gt; are pleased to announce the immediate release of &lt;strong&gt;Apache Nutch v1.20&lt;/strong&gt;, we advise all current users and developers of the 1.X series to upgrade to this release.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div id=&#34;action-buttons&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;button primary big&#34; href=&#34;/download&#34; onclick=&#34;_gaq.push([&#39;_trackEvent&#39;, &#39;kube&#39;, &#39;download&#39;]);&#34;&gt;Download Nutch 1.20&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;You may also be interested in the &lt;a href=&#34;https://s.apache.org/lf6li&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34;&gt;1.20 release report&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In the 1.X series, release artifacts are made available as both source and binary and also available within &lt;a href=&#34;https://search.maven.org/search?q=g:org.apache.nutch%20AND%20a:nutch%20AND%20v:1.20&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34;&gt;Maven Central&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
